1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:07,080
Today I'll show you how to design a piece of furniture made to measure for your home, straight from a hand sketch, and without any CAD knowledge.

2
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:13,440
At the end, you'll have a 3D model, workshop drawings with all dimensions, and a cut list for the timber yard.

3
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:20,156
We use SOMA for this.

4
00:00:20,156 --> 00:00:24,260
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

5
00:00:25,210 --> 00:00:28,465
I start with a new model, saved as Sideboard.

6
00:00:28,465 --> 00:00:30,996
The design work is done by SOMA AI:

7
00:00:30,996 --> 00:00:34,540
I click its tab, and pick the model, GPT-6.1 Sol.

8
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:37,091
SOMA itself is free.

9
00:00:37,091 --> 00:00:39,789
For SOMA AI, you bring your own AI:

10
00:00:39,789 --> 00:00:42,640
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

11
00:00:43,617 --> 00:00:46,934
My sketch is on paper, and a photo from the phone is enough.

12
00:00:46,934 --> 00:00:49,587
Click Import, and it goes into the model folder.

13
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:51,680
Click it to open it.

14
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:53,346
Here it is:

15
00:00:53,346 --> 00:00:59,720
a low shelf on casters, 80 centimetres wide and 60 high, with a middle shelf and two compartments.

16
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:02,423
Send it to SOMA AI.

17
00:01:02,423 --> 00:01:05,140
It goes into the chat, ready for my message.

18
00:01:06,090 --> 00:01:08,834
Now describe in plain words what you want.

19
00:01:08,834 --> 00:01:10,140
No CAD terms needed.

20
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:19,560
SOMA AI looks at the sketch first.

21
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:21,477
If something is unclear, it asks.

22
00:01:21,477 --> 00:01:24,034
I click the answers that fit, and send them.

23
00:01:31,184 --> 00:01:33,732
Then it plans the boards and builds the model.

24
00:01:33,732 --> 00:01:36,114
This takes a few minutes, here much faster.

25
00:01:37,484 --> 00:01:38,491
And here it is:

26
00:01:38,491 --> 00:01:40,976
a real panel construction in plywood.

27
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:48,094
Sides, top and bottom, the middle shelf and dividers, a thin back panel, and placeholders for the casters.

28
00:01:49,044 --> 00:01:51,966
Every board is its own part in the structure tree.

29
00:01:51,966 --> 00:01:55,414
Click one in the 3D view, and SOMA shows which board it is.

30
00:01:56,364 --> 00:01:59,676
To look at the model, SOMA has viewing tools that change nothing.

31
00:01:59,676 --> 00:02:03,294
Explode pulls the boards apart, so you see how the shelf goes together.

32
00:02:09,884 --> 00:02:11,954
For the workshop, I need drawings.

33
00:02:11,954 --> 00:02:13,294
I simply ask for them.

34
00:02:20,684 --> 00:02:23,533
SOMA AI lays out every board with its dimensions.

35
00:02:25,184 --> 00:02:26,804
They appear in the Drawings tab:

36
00:02:26,804 --> 00:02:31,714
the views with all the main dimensions, ready to print, or to take into the workshop on a tablet.

37
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:48,789
Next, the cut list.

38
00:02:48,789 --> 00:02:54,434
I ask for an Excel file with every board, its size and edge banding, and a shopping list.

39
00:03:00,984 --> 00:03:03,834
SOMA AI writes the file, and reads it back to check it.

40
00:03:05,084 --> 00:03:07,147
The file lands in the model folder.

41
00:03:07,147 --> 00:03:08,974
Open it in any spreadsheet app.

42
00:03:11,984 --> 00:03:17,474
The cut list has every board with length, width, thickness and quantity, and how its edges are finished.

43
00:03:18,917 --> 00:03:24,612
The shopping list has the plywood, the casters, screws, glue and finish, and even the tools to check.

44
00:03:24,612 --> 00:03:26,247
Ready for the hardware store.

45
00:03:29,684 --> 00:03:31,705
Now, the shelf should be wider.

46
00:03:31,705 --> 00:03:34,573
SOMA AI made the main dimensions adjustable:

47
00:03:34,573 --> 00:03:36,919
you find them in the Parameters tab.

48
00:03:39,484 --> 00:03:42,931
Click the width, and drag it from 80 to 100 centimetres.

49
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:44,715
The model updates right away.

50
00:03:44,715 --> 00:03:46,254
No agent needed for this.

51
00:03:47,884 --> 00:03:51,294
The height works the same way, and so does everything else in this list.

52
00:03:59,217 --> 00:04:00,144
One more wish:

53
00:04:00,144 --> 00:04:01,800
a door for the left side.

54
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,649
Click Mark up, and draw right on the model:

55
00:04:04,649 --> 00:04:07,166
the outline of the door, and a handle.

56
00:04:10,617 --> 00:04:14,107
Then an arrow, and a word, so SOMA AI knows what I mean.

57
00:04:18,384 --> 00:04:20,674
Send it to SOMA AI, with one sentence.

58
00:04:27,950 --> 00:04:30,105
SOMA AI first asks which hinges I have.

59
00:04:30,105 --> 00:04:36,240
Then it builds the door with a wooden pull and two hinges, and brings the drawings and the cut list up to date.

60
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:39,760
Here is the door, with its wooden pull.

61
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:43,300
The two hinges are placeholders until I pick real ones.

62
00:04:47,850 --> 00:04:50,540
The drawings show the door, and the new width of one metre.

63
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:02,803
Every board has its own sheet, and now the door and the pull have one too.

64
00:05:06,383 --> 00:05:10,264
And the shopping list now has the hinges, a door catch and two bumpers.

65
00:05:12,716 --> 00:05:13,263
That's it:

66
00:05:13,263 --> 00:05:19,006
from a hand sketch to a 3D model, workshop drawings and a cut list, without drawing a single line in CAD.

67
00:05:19,956 --> 00:05:23,246
This was a simple, quick example to show how SOMA works.

68
00:05:23,246 --> 00:05:27,827
With a bit more time, you can design complex pieces of furniture the same way.

69
00:05:27,827 --> 00:05:29,766
Get SOMA for free at somacad.app.
